hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan in today's  episode I'm going to answer question  from one of my newsletter readers Chris  who wants to create a five-year business  plan and one of my advice on how to do  it so Chris I think the first thing you  need to figure out is who is your reader  so are you doing this to try to raise  money for your business or is it just  for you to be able to plan your company  so if you're doing it to raise money for  going after you know an angel investor  or venture capital or banks when I was  in the VC business the first thing we  looked at was the executive summary so  quick summary of what your business did  then we look at the management team and  saw you know who's behind this operation  do we think that they can they can do it  they can excel and then we poured over  the financials and see what kind of  projections they had going forward and  then everything else so those would be  the first three things that I would  really make sure our super solid is your  executive summary your management team  bios and your financials and be able to  explain every number on there every word  that comes out of there because you're  going to get grilled on those sections  more than any other section in your  business plan it was just for you if  it's for you to plan your own business  and the in the next five years and where  you want to grow I would start around  know what is the vision for your company  so where do you see yourself going what  what's the main private service you want  to launch and how do you see it helping  people and how can you help the most  number of people in the most meaningful  way and start with that kind of bigger  vision for your business and then you  can start get into the execution so you  in five years where do you see yourself  where do you want your business to be  and then what do you need to do to be  able to get your business there so  you're going to be doing a lot do you  need to bring on team members to help  you how you going to actually execute it  so the execution is your marketing your  production you know all the costs that  come along with it people you might need  to hire to be able to get you you know  where you need to go but you start  around the big goal that you have so  your company in five years and you start  working towards that goal if you're a  brand new startup then it can be really  hard to do a five-year plan it's still  great to do it's an awesome exercise to  go through it teaches you a lot about  the market and how to  your business the reality is your  business mind is going to change you  know almost from day one as you start  your business if it's a brand new  business and you have to be flexible  with it so you'll make multiple updates  to your business plan as you continue to  grow you want to build around your  customers figure out what the challenges  are you get as close as you can to them  as possible get feedback from them and  incorporate that into your future  business Pine Grove so it's good to have  the five year plan it's good to have a  big goal for yourself a vision is shoot  for just be flexible because what you  think you're going to be what processor  is you think you're going to come up  with are going to change the further out  the future you go the more things are  going to change so keep coming back to  your business plan you can look at it  every quarter to see how you're doing  and potentially make changes based on  new information you've learned by  talking to customers actually going out  there and making sales so I hope that  helps if you guys like the video please  give it a thumbs up below and it also  love to hear you have to think if you  want to leave a comment or if you have a  question put that below in the comments  and we'll see you on the next episode  you
 

